{title: We’re Marching to Zion}
{artist: Isaac Watts / Robert Lowry}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Upbeat}
{flow: Opening}
{key: F}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Broadman Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: Broadman Press, 1940), # 8)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Come, we that [C7]love the [F]Lord,
[F]And let our joys be [C]known;
[C]Join [F]in a song with [Bb]sweet accord,
[Bb]Join [C]in a song with [G7]sweet accord
[G7]And [F]thus [C]sur[F]round the throne,
[F]And [C7]thus surround the [F]throne.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]We’re marching to Zion,
[F]Beautiful, beautiful [C]Zion;
[C]We’re [F]marching upward to [Bb]Zion,
[Bb]The [C7]beautiful city of [F]God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]The sorrows [C7]of the [F]mind
[F]Be banished from the [C]place;
[C]Re[F]ligion never [Bb]was designed
[Bb]Re[C]ligion never [G7]was designed,
[G7]To [F]make [C]our [F]pleasures less,
[F]To [C7]make our pleasures [F]less.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Let those re[C7]fuse to [F]sing,
[F]Who never knew our [C]God;
[C]But [F]favorites of the [Bb]heav’nly King,
[Bb]But [C]favorites of the [G7]heav’nly King
[G7]May [F]speak [C]their [F]joys abroad,
[F]May [C7]speak their joys a[F]broad.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]The God that [C7]rules on [F]high,
[F]And thunders when He [C]please,
[C]Who [F]rides upon the [Bb]stormy sky,
[Bb]Who [C]rides upon the [G7]stormy sky,
[G7]And [F]man[C]ag[F]es the seas,
[F]And [C7]manages the [F]seas.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]This awful [C7]God is [F]ours,
[F]Our Father and our [C]Love;
[C]He [F]will send down His [Bb]heav’nly powers,
[Bb]He [C]will send down His [G7]heav’nly powers,
[G7]To [F]car[C]ry [F]us above,
[F]To [C7]carry us a[F]bove.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[F]There we shall [C7]see His [F]face,
[F]And never, never [C]sin!
[C]There, [F]from the rivers [Bb]of His grace,
[Bb]There, [C]from the rivers [G7]of His grace,
[G7]Drink [F]end[C]less [F]pleasures in,
[F]Drink [C7]endless pleasures [F]in.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[F]The hill of [C7]Zion [F]yields
[F]A thousand sacred [C]sweets
[C]Be[F]fore we reach the [Bb]heav’nly fields,
[Bb]Be[C]fore we reach the [G7]heav’nly fields,
[G7]Or [F]walk [C]the [F]golden streets,
[F]Or [C7]walk the golden [F]streets.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
[F]Then let our [C7]songs a[F]bound,
[F]And every tear be [C]dry;
[C]We’re [F]marching through Im[Bb]manuel’s ground,
[Bb]We’re [C]marching through Im[G7]manuel’s ground,
[G7]To [F]fair[C]er [F]worlds on high,
[F]To [C7]fairer worlds on [F]high.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
